  "worked_solution": "First, multiplying each component of $c$ by $-\\frac{1}{3}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}c & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{1}{3}c)\\cdot d & =0\\cdot 9+2\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =0+8+8-3-6 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
